@startuml
title Canonical Tick — candidate / commit / publication
hide footbox
autonumber
participant "Protocol & Replication" as Protocol
participant "Simulation\n(authoritative coordinator)" as Sim
participant "Scenario / Session Lifecycle" as Owners
participant "Reconstruction evidence" as Evidence
participant "Committed-view consumers" as Views
Protocol -> Sim : eligible Intentions
Sim -> Sim : seal intake; stable ordering
Sim -> Owners : derive candidate effects
Owners --> Sim : candidate effects (not published)
Sim -> Evidence : reserve mandatory reconstruction capacity
alt candidate rejected before commit
  Sim -> Sim : discard candidate; no Tick/time/state advance
  note over Sim,Evidence : Mandatory reconstruction-capacity failure\nterminates the session; it is not silent data loss.
else candidate can commit
  group one authoritative commit point
    Sim -> Sim : commit state + Tick + Simulated Time\n+ events + reconstruction record atomically
  end
  alt publication succeeds
    Sim -> Views : publish immutable committed version
  else failure after commit
    Sim -> Sim : complete publication OR terminate technical failure
    note over Sim,Views : Never roll back the committed Tick\nor expose a partially authoritative Tick.
  end
end
note over Protocol,Views
  The Tick never waits for clients, Observability or external export.
  Prediction and Presentation run independently and cannot author outcomes.
end note
@enduml
